# Guild NPCs (design/data/npcs.toml, economy/guild_npcs.js) and the Fuze / desk split of the bounty board.
# `ttl guild npc expect <field> <value>` and `ttl guild expect ...` print "ttl: ..." when the value is wrong, which
# `server.sh test-all` counts as a failure.
# Needs Tempest placed (the receptionist and the stand-in Fuze stand in its council longhouse) and Easy NPC with the
# presets from config/easy_npc/preset and `ttl` in config/easy_npc/security.cfg executeAsUserCommandAllowList.ALL.
# Bot A is a Life 2 soul (test hook), bot B stays in Life 1. A bot standing at a spot loads its chunk.
# Expect in the log: "[ttl] guild npc: receptionist_tempest (receptionist) spawned at ...", "... had 2 copies, 1 removed",
# and no "[ttl] guild npc: importing ... failed" or "economy command failed". Needs Blumund placed too (its spots
# fuze_blumund, receptionist_blumund_1/2 take over from the Tempest Fuze stand-in).
ttlbot spawn TtlBotNpcA
ttlbot spawn TtlBotNpcB
@sleep 2
ttl guild test TtlBotNpcA life2
ttl guild reset TtlBotNpcA
# (`ttl guild npc expect presets true` checks that the preset files are on the server; it answers n/a if KubeJS may not read files.)
# ---- split of the board: Fuze's contracts are only rank B and up, the desk's only below ----
ttl guild roll
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA board 5
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA board_desk 5
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA board_fuze 2
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA board_all 7
ttl guild npc expect fuze_board_size 2
ttl guild npc expect fuze_board_high true
ttl guild npc expect desk_board_low true
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA giver_rabbit_cull desk
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA giver_fz_ender_watch fuze
# Hand-in (owner 18/11/2026): the desk (and the plain `turnin`) takes Fuze's finished contracts too, except a contract
# with a lore implication (economy.toml `lore = true`: the ogre village, the Dwarven Crown's magisteel), which only Fuze
# takes; Fuze never takes the desk's bounties. The rule only, no hand-in happens here.
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA turnin_desk_fz_ender_watch allowed
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA turnin_any_fz_ender_watch allowed
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA turnin_desk_fz_ogre_ruin lore
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA turnin_any_fz_magisteel_shipment lore
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA turnin_fuze_fz_ogre_ruin allowed
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA turnin_fuze_rabbit_cull wrong_giver
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA turnin_desk_rabbit_cull allowed
# A rank F soul sees Fuze's contract but cannot take it ("rank"); a desk contract is not Fuze's to give and a Fuze
# contract is not the desk's ("wrong_giver"); Life 1 is refused whoever asks.
ttl guild post fz_ender_watch
ttl guild post rabbit_cull
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA take_fuze_fz_ender_watch rank
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA take_desk_fz_ender_watch wrong_giver
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA take_fuze_rabbit_cull wrong_giver
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcB take_fuze_fz_ender_watch life2only
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcB take_desk_rabbit_cull life2only
# The desk lets her take rabbit_cull (a real take, undone at once); her board never shows Fuze's contracts.
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA take_desk_rabbit_cull allowed
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA accepted_rabbit_cull true
execute as TtlBotNpcA run ttl guild abandon rabbit_cull
ttl guild expect TtlBotNpcA accepted_rabbit_cull false
execute as TtlBotNpcA run ttl guild board desk
execute as TtlBotNpcA run ttl guild board fuze
# ---- placement: exactly one of each ----
ttl guild npc list
# A bot that was teleported within one dimension does not make its new chunk entity-ticking (it sends no movement
# packets; in game 18/11/2026), so the two Tempest spots are force-loaded for the test (removed again at the end).
execute in minecraft:overworld run forceload add ${anchor:tempest.x+3} ${anchor:tempest.z-19} ${anchor:tempest.x+8} ${anchor:tempest.z-16}
ttl guild npc goto TtlBotNpcA receptionist_tempest
@sleep 4
ttl guild npc remove receptionist_tempest
ttl guild npc expect count_receptionist_tempest 0
ttl guild npc ensure receptionist_tempest
ttl guild npc expect count_receptionist_tempest 1
ttl guild npc expect tags_receptionist_tempest ok
# Idempotent: another check changes nothing.
ttl guild npc ensure receptionist_tempest
ttl guild npc expect count_receptionist_tempest 1
# An extra copy (test hook) is removed again by the next check.
ttl guild npc spawn receptionist_tempest
ttl guild npc expect count_receptionist_tempest 2
ttl guild npc ensure receptionist_tempest
ttl guild npc expect count_receptionist_tempest 1
# Fuze: Blumund is placed (on staging and at launch every canon build is), so he stands in Blumund's guild hall and the
# Tempest stand-in spot is inactive (`unless_build = "blumund"`). Blumund's spots are force-loaded like Tempest's: Fuze's stand
# is Blumund's placed anchor + (45, 6, -11), and the placer surveys up to 128 blocks round the `blumund` anchor, so no fixed box
# holds it; `ttl cast load` force-loads the chunk of every active spot where it really stands (released again at the end).
ttl cast load
ttl guild npc goto TtlBotNpcA fuze_blumund
@sleep 4
ttl guild npc remove fuze_blumund
ttl guild npc ensure fuze_blumund
ttl guild npc expect count_fuze_blumund 1
ttl guild npc expect tags_fuze_blumund ok
ttl guild npc spawn fuze_blumund
ttl guild npc ensure fuze_blumund
ttl guild npc expect count_fuze_blumund 1
ttl guild npc ensure fuze_tempest
ttl guild npc expect count_fuze_tempest 0
# By kind: one Fuze, and one receptionist per enabled spot of the receptionist kind (tag ttl.npc.receptionist.<n>).
ttl guild npc ensure
ttl guild npc expect count_fuze 1
ttl guild npc expect count_receptionist_blumund_1 1
ttl guild npc expect count_receptionist_blumund_2 1
# Clean up: the NPCs stay (they are the real ones); only the bots go.
ttl guild reset TtlBotNpcA
ttl guild npc ensure
execute in minecraft:overworld run forceload remove ${anchor:tempest.x+3} ${anchor:tempest.z-19} ${anchor:tempest.x+8} ${anchor:tempest.z-16}
ttl cast unload
ttlbot remove TtlBotNpcA
ttlbot remove TtlBotNpcB
